+---
+id: task-002-rental-module-availability-query
+type: task
+title: "Rental module: availability query"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Rental module: availability query
+
+The desk needs to see at a glance what can still be rented.
+
+## Requested behaviour
+
+Add `availability(query)` to the rental service, where `query` is `{ start, end, kind }` and `kind` is optional.
+It returns the ids of the equipment of that kind, or of any kind when `kind` is not given, that is free for the
+whole period, sorted.
+
+## Interpretation
+
+- `start` and `end` follow the same rules as `quote` and `book`: midnight UTC, `end` strictly after `start`.
+  Invalid periods throw.
+- `kind`, when given, must be `'board'` or `'sail'`; any other value throws, as `addEquipment` does.
+- An item is free when no booking of it overlaps the period. Periods are half-open `[start, end)`, so a booking
+  that ends where the period starts (or starts where it ends) does not make the item unavailable.
+- The result is the item ids sorted in ascending code-unit order (default `Array.prototype.sort` on strings), so
+  it is deterministic. No match gives an empty array.
+- `availability` does not change any state.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- Lists all equipment when `kind` is omitted, and only the given kind when it is set.
+- Excludes items with an overlapping booking; keeps items with only adjacent bookings.
+- Returns ids sorted, regardless of insertion order.
+- Returns an empty array when nothing is free.
+- Throws for an invalid period and for an invalid kind.
+- Tests are deterministic and in-process, with no external services.
